{"id": "EUVD-2026-108654", "enisaUuid": "bbbf7035-21bd-36bf-80d8-dddfe63fa07b", "description": "`HmacShaCryptor.Hash` never hashed its input. For any input it returned `HMAC_K(\"\")` \u2014 the MAC of the empty message under the key. Every AES-CBC-HMAC JWE produced or verified by gose therefore carried an authentication tag that is constant per key and independent of the message, removing ciphertext integrity entirely.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T08:56:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T08:56:20", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/eclipse-keypont/gose/security/advisories/GHSA-h6w5-722x-2h3m"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89320"], "assigner": "eclipse", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "36e6602b-5a16-3b4d-85c1-50d7937dd254", "product": {"name": "Eclipse KeyPont - GOSE", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0.9.0 \u22640.13.0-rc1"}, {"id": "829a3c9b-1077-34ae-8311-305156eb7368", "product": {"name": "Eclipse KeyPont - GOSE", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.0.0-rc1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f651c937-6557-37e5-b5a7-c714be582467", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}